flowchart TB
  accTitle: Which runner the AI runs on
  accDescr: The job event reads the repository variable ISSUE_ASSISTANT_AI_RUNNER. Unset, or ubuntu-24.04-firewall, the job analyze runs on GitHub's egress-firewall runner, whose firewall blocks every host but those of .github/egress-firewall.yaml for the whole machine. For one of GitHub's runners of Ubuntu with a fixed version, such as ubuntu-24.04, the job event names the hosts of the same file with their ports; there Harden-Runner blocks every other host as the first step of analyze, and the next step stops the job when requests to example.com still get through after a minute, before the engine runs. For any other runner, such as a self-hosted one or ubuntu-latest, the job event fails and the AI doesn't run.
  variable["`the variable<br>**ISSUE_ASSISTANT_AI_RUNNER**`"]
  variable -->|"unset, or ubuntu-24.04-firewall"| firewall
  variable -->|"ubuntu-24.04 and the like"| endpoints
  variable -->|"self-hosted, ubuntu-latest, …"| refused
  subgraph preview ["ubuntu-24.04-firewall, a technical preview"]
    firewall["`**analyze**<br>GitHub's firewall blocks every other host<br>for the whole machine`"]
  end
  endpoints["`**event** names the hosts of<br>egress-firewall.yaml, on 443 and 80`"]
  subgraph plain ["ubuntu-24.04"]
    hardened["`**analyze**<br>Harden-Runner blocks every other host<br>for the job`"]
    holds["`do requests to example.com<br>still get through after a minute?`"]
    hardened --> holds
  end
  endpoints --> hardened
  firewall --> engine(["the engine runs"])
  holds -->|no| engine
  holds -->|yes| stop(["the job stops,<br>the AI doesn't run"])
  refused(["event fails,<br>the AI doesn't run"])
  classDef ai fill:#8250df33,stroke:#8250df,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef safe fill:#1a7f3726,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:2px
  classDef untrusted fill:#cf222e26,stroke:#cf222e,stroke-width:2px
  class firewall,hardened ai
  class variable,endpoints,holds job
  class engine safe
  class stop,refused untrusted
